### Installation & Run Locally
```bash
# Clone repo
git clone https://github.com/MaryamArif85/Research-Paper-Assistant-RAG
cd Research-Paper-Assistant-RAG

# Create venv
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate  # Windows
# source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Create .env file
echo GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here > .env

# Run
uvicorn main:app --reload
Open: localhost:8000

Create .env file:

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_google_gemini_api_key

Get key from: aistudio.google.com

### How It Works
1. User uploads PDFs -> Saved to `/tmp/uploads` (Vercel compatible)
2. Text extracted with page numbers
3. Text chunked (1000 chars) and embedded via Gemini Embeddings
4. Stored in FAISS in-memory vector store
5. User asks question -> Similarity search retrieves relevant chunks
6. Chunks + Question -> Gemini LLM generates answer with citations

### Deployment Fixes (Important for Vercel)
- Uses `/tmp` directory for uploads (Vercel serverless is read-only)
- `TemplateResponse` with `request` parameter to avoid auto-wrapping bug
- Lightweight dependencies to stay under 500MB limit
- Handles `FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED` by proper error handling

### API Endpoints
- `GET /` - Home page
- `POST /upload` - Upload PDFs
- `POST /ask` - Ask question to your papers

